  "hypothesis": "JS bound clamping and method delegation may alter callback eligibility or order compared with C isok/getbounds/getpoint iteration.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Only valid x>0 selected map points invoke callbacks, in x-major/y-minor order; iteration does not mutate the selection.",
  "observedBehavior": "Exact C iteration plus allocation/read/write/bounds helpers matches production JS iteration for all1680 singleton cells and64 subsets of six boundary points. Callback coordinates and order match, column0 is skipped, and JS input maps remain unchanged. Both use absolute selections and no origin conversion. This is a finite proof, not equivalence for arbitrary selections or alternate origins.",
